Kind: ablation
Issue: #780
Takes out: the three tails' fresh start -- thread_exception_return, thread_bootstrap_return and restart_mach_syscall no longer put %rsp back at kernel_stack, so every exception act_test's arm seventeen answers with "resume" comes back through the tail one level deeper on the kernel stack, a hundred times.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Expect: UrMach x86-64: trap (general protection|double fault|page fault)|act_test: \[17\] [0-9]+ of 100 exceptions arrived
Note: both accelerators: the canonical check that sends the thread round again is the kernel's, not the processor's.  The stack runs out before the hundredth round, and either the kernel reports the fault it ends in or the arm counts fewer than a hundred.

